---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Breadcrumb from "@/components/Breadcrumb.astro";
import Main from "@/components/Main.astro";
import config from "@/config";

const pageTitle = "Cookie Policy & Consent Governance";
const pageDescription =
  "How Red Sun Japan uses cookies, local storage, and three-tier granular consent. What stays active by default, what stays off, and how to revoke your choices at any time.";

const contactEmail = "contact@redsunjapan.com";
const contactMailto = `mailto:${contactEmail}?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Cookie & Consent Question")}`;
---

<Layout
  title={`${pageTitle} | ${config.site.title}`}
  description={pageDescription}
>
  <Header />

  <Breadcrumb />

  <Main pageTitle={pageTitle} class="app-prose">
    <p class="lead italic text-[#928f88]">
      Last Updated: October 15, 2026. This page explains the cookies and
      similar storage that Red Sun Japan uses, what each one does, and how
      to change your mind at any time.
    </p>

    <div
      class="not-prose my-6 rounded-lg border border-[#27272a] bg-[#161619] p-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[#928f88]"
    >
      <strong class="text-[#e2ded7]">Short version:</strong>
      we use only the cookies strictly necessary to run the site (theme
      preference, CSRF protection, your saved consent choice). Analytics
      and marketing cookies stay
      <strong class="text-[#e2ded7]">off by default</strong>
      and only load if you explicitly opt in. You can revoke that choice
      from the
      <strong class="text-[#e2ded7]">"Manage Cookie Preferences"</strong>
      button in the footer of any page.
    </div>

    <h2>1. What is a cookie?</h2>
    <p>
      A cookie is a small text file your browser stores on your device
      when you visit a site. Cookies (and the closely related
      <em>localStorage</em> and <em>sessionStorage</em> APIs) let a site
      remember small pieces of state between page loads: your theme
      preference, your language, whether you've already seen a notice,
      and so on. They cannot run code on your device or read other
      files on it.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use the word "cookie" throughout this page to mean both
      traditional cookies and equivalent client-side storage
      (localStorage, sessionStorage, IndexedDB). The consent architecture
      is the same for all of them.
    </p>

    <h2>2. The three-tier consent architecture</h2>
    <p>
      We follow a strict <strong>three-tier model</strong>. Each tier is
      independent, meaning accepting one does not automatically opt you
      into the others:
    </p>

    <h3>Tier 1 — Strictly Necessary (always active)</h3>
    <p>
      These storage items are required for the site to function and
      cannot be switched off in our systems. They are set without
      consent because the site cannot operate without them.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Theme preference (Dark / Light mode):</strong> a small
        localStorage entry that remembers your visual choice across
        pages and visits.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cookie consent record:</strong> a localStorage entry
        that stores the choices you made in the consent banner so we
        don't show the banner again on every visit.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cryptographic state tokens:</strong> short-lived
        session tokens that protect form submissions against cross-site
        request forgery (CSRF). These are cleared when you close the
        browser tab.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Pagefind search index:</strong> a small client-side
        index that powers the search page. It is generated locally and
        is not transmitted to any server.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Tier 2 — Analytics & Telemetry (off by default)</h3>
    <p>
      We may load aggregate, anonymized analytics to understand which
      articles resonate and where the site is slow. This data is never
      tied to your name, email, or any other personal identifier; it
      is also never sold or shared with third parties for advertising.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Privacy-respecting analytics tooling (when enabled) records
        only: anonymized IP fragment, browser family, device class,
        referrer, and the article URL visited.
      </li>
      <li>
        No cross-site profiling, no fingerprinting, no persistent user
        identifiers.
      </li>
      <li>
        You can opt out at any time via the
        <strong>"Manage Cookie Preferences"</strong> button in the
        footer.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Tier 3 — Marketing & Third-Party Embeds (off by default)</h3>
    <p>
      We may load marketing pixels or advertising tags that evaluate
      media engagement, retarget visitors, or measure ad performance.
      These are loaded
      <strong>only after explicit opt-in</strong>
      and never before.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Examples of tags that may load under Tier 3: Google AdSense,
        Pinterest tag, Facebook Pixel, affiliate network trackers.
      </li>
      <li>
        These tags are operated by their respective vendors and are
        subject to those vendors' privacy policies — see the
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> Section 4 for the list
        of third parties we partner with.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. The consent banner</h2>
    <p>
      The first time you visit Red Sun Japan, a banner appears at the
      bottom of the page with three equally weighted options:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Accept All</strong> — enables Tier 2 and Tier 3 in
        addition to Tier 1.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reject All</strong> — keeps only Tier 1 active.
        Analytics and marketing tags are not loaded.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Customize</strong> — opens a detailed panel where you
        can enable or disable Tier 2 and Tier 3 independently.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Your choice is stored in a localStorage record (a Tier 1 item)
      and respected on every subsequent visit. The banner does not
      reappear unless you clear your browser storage or revoke your
      choice from the footer.
    </p>

    <h2>4. How to change or revoke your choice</h2>
    <p>
      You can review, modify, or completely revoke your cookie consent
      selections at any time. Two methods are supported:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Click the
        <strong class="text-[#e2ded7]">"Manage Cookie Preferences"</strong>
        link in the footer of any page. This reopens the consent
        banner with your current choices pre-selected.
      </li>
      <li>
        Clear your browser's site data for
        <code class="text-xs bg-[#222227] px-1 py-0.5 rounded"
          >redsunjapan.com</code
        >. The next page load will treat you as a new visitor and show
        the banner again.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Either action is immediate. No data collected under a previous
      choice is retroactively deleted, but no further data will be
      collected under the new choice.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Third-party storage set by content we embed</h2>
    <p>
      Even when marketing cookies are disabled, the act of
      <em>clicking play</em>
      on an embedded video can cause the third-party platform to set its
      own cookies. We mitigate this by using the most privacy-respecting
      embed mode available:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>YouTube videos</strong> are embedded via
        <code class="text-xs bg-[#222227] px-1 py-0.5 rounded"
          >youtube-nocookie.com</code
        >. YouTube does not set tracking cookies until you actively
        press play.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Pagefind search</strong> runs entirely in your browser;
        no data is sent to any external service.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Coolify / hosting infrastructure</strong> may write
        short-lived server logs (anonymized IP, request path, status
        code) retained for at most 30 days for DDoS protection and
        security monitoring.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Your rights under GDPR, CCPA, LGPD & APPI</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have additional rights
      related to cookies and tracking:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to refuse non-essential cookies</strong> — we
        honor this by keeping Tier 2 and Tier 3 off by default.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to access</strong> what data has been collected
        about you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to erasure</strong> ("right to be forgotten") of
        any personal data we hold.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to data portability</strong> in a machine-readable
        format.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, write to
      <a href={contactMailto}>{contactEmail}</a>. We respond within the
      statutory deadlines for your jurisdiction (typically 30 days for
      GDPR, 45 days for CCPA).
    </p>

    <h2>7. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We will update this page if we change which cookies we use, add
      new tiers, or change the consent flow. Material changes will be
      reflected in the "Last Updated" date at the top of this page and
      may trigger a re-prompt of the consent banner on your next visit.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Questions</h2>
    <p>
      If anything on this page is unclear, or you want to know exactly
      which cookies were set during a specific visit, write to
      <a href={contactMailto}>{contactEmail}</a> with the date and time
      of the visit (taken from your browser history) and we will pull
      the server log.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p class="text-sm text-[#928f88]">
      For the full legal framework that governs cookies, data
      processing, and your rights, see the
      <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      For information on commercial relationships and editorial
      standards, see the
      <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>.
    </p>
  </Main>
</Layout>
